          "title": "The word, taken apart — a documented source",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Punjabi University's Punjabipedia explicitly records English Class as the source of modern written ਕਲਾਸ (kalaas). It also lists several meanings; this lesson keeps only the bounded school class-or-grade meaning. The Punjabi school noun comes from English Class. Source: Punjabi University Punjabipedia."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The Punjab School Education Board's current circular page uses the word in school scheduling prose. That current school use supports the narrow meaning here. The deeper history and other meanings stay outside this lesson. Source: Punjab School Education Board."
            }
          ]
        },
